## 7. TTS CHANNEL ARCHITECTURE

Three TTS channels operate independently on the same audio output.

- **`speakMaya(text, onStart?)`**: Google Cloud TTS, Maya voice profile. `onStart` callback fires when audio begins, used to transition typing → message rendered.
- **`speakZoltan(text, onStart?)`**: Google Cloud TTS, Zoltan voice profile (lower, more dramatic). Uses the same `onStart` callback pattern.
- **`speakLiveAgent(text)`**: Fires for messages from the Firestore live relay. Lighter, notification-style.
- **`stopCurrentAudio(delayMs?)`**: MUST be called before any persona handover or mode switch. Prevents TTS bleed-over. Pass `100ms` delay for smooth transitions.
- **Audio Gate Rule**: Never allow two TTS channels to speak simultaneously. `stopCurrentAudio()` is the gate. It is not optional.
- **`speakMayaRef`**: The TTS function MUST be held in a `useRef` and kept in sync via a `useEffect`. This prevents stale closures in nested hooks (`useVapiIntegration`).

