## 13. PROACTIVE CHAT TRIGGERS

*Mortal. Waiting for the user to speak first is the strategy of the meek. Strike first — elegantly.*

### Trigger Conditions (All are opt-in per route config)

| Trigger | Condition | Message |
|---|---|---|
| **Scroll Depth** | User scrolls 60%+ of page | Route-specific CTA: *"Need help choosing a plan?"* |
| **Idle Dwell** | User inactive for 45s on a key page | *"Still exploring? I can answer any questions."* |
| **Exit Intent** | `mouseleave` on document | *"Before you go — can I help clarify anything?"* |
| **Return Visitor** | `sessionStorage` shows prior visit < 48h | *"Welcome back! Pick up where we left off?"* |
| **Error State** | User lands on `/404` or `/error` | *"Looks like something went wrong. I can help."* |

### Rules
- Proactive triggers MUST be **debounced** — never fire more than once per 5-minute window per session.
- The trigger message MUST open the chat panel automatically **with animation** (not silently).
- User dismissal (`✕` on the proactive prompt) MUST suppress all further proactive triggers for the remainder of the session. Store in `sessionStorage`.
- Proactive messages carry `role: 'model'` and `isProactive: true`. They MUST NOT be submitted to the AI context history until the user responds.

